{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And now lest he send his hand.</b> It is a short verse — <b>and now</b> — it is fitting that he be banished from here, lest he send his hand, since all is in the hands of heaven except fear of heaven. And now, lest he send his hand — it is revealed and known before Him that even within the garden the Holy One, blessed be He, could guard the man so that he would not take from the tree of life; but corresponding to the attribute of judgment, which would prosecute against him to test him, as it is written — and it was revealed before Him that if he were tested he would not withstand the trial; therefore He acted for him beyond the line of justice to banish him from there, so as to have an opening to say: even had he remained there, he would not have violated His command." "<b>And take also from the tree of life.</b> After he grew accustomed to transgress and eat from the tree of knowledge, he would breach the fence of the tree of life and eat from it. And furthermore, he was warned only concerning the tree of knowledge." "<b>And eat and live forever.</b> And if you ask: is it not written above, ״for on the day you eat of it you shall surely die״, and behold he transgressed the command and ate from it, so how could he live forever? One may answer: the tree of life was an elixir of life and a remedy for one who ate from the tree of knowledge — for if you do not say so, but rather he would literally die, then after his death he would have no ability to eat from the tree of life. Therefore the tree of life was created only to remedy the harm of the tree of knowledge, and ״you shall surely die״ means: he shall be reckoned as dead. Another interpretation: the Holy One, blessed be He, said: death has already been decreed upon him, and I have decreed concerning the tree of life that all who eat from it shall live forever. If the man eats from it, how can these two decrees both stand? Therefore it is right that I banish him from the Garden of Eden. Another interpretation: if he begets children inside the garden, they would not sin, to have death decreed upon them, and if they eat from the tree of life they would live forever; therefore He banished him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:55.679165345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}